            <ArticleTitle>[Mitral valve prolapse in patients with coronary artery insufficiency. Report of two unusual cases (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>801-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors illustrate two peculiar cases of mitral valve prolapse in patients with coronary artery disease. The first case reports a mitral valve prolapse that, absent in basal conditions, is unmasked by a premature ventricular beat. In the second case concerns about the manifestation of a mitral valve prolapse developed during the course of retrosternal chest pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
